a System (USRDS) is a surveillance system for ESRD\"}]}], \"methods_quotes\": [{\"loc\": \"summary\", \"q\": \"Rates were age-adjusted based on the 2000 U.S. standard population.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"ESRD-D incidence rates were age-adjusted based on the 2000 U.S. standard population, and joinpoint regression was used to analyze trends\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Each trend segment is described by an annual percentage change (APC) with a 95% confidence interval (CI)\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"The rate of change for linear trends was tested to determine whether it was significantly different from zero.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"ESRD-D incidence was calculated using the number of newly treated ESRD-D cases and two population estimates\"}], \"confidence\": \"medium\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"study_design\"]}", "type": "text"}]}